STGR PATCH: 0001 — Branding strings and upstream attribution
Purpose:                Identify the product as "STGR Browser" and always attribute the
                        upstream base as "Based on Mozilla Firefox". Most visual branding
                        (name, icons, installer, version strings) is handled by the
                        --with-branding directory (stgr/build/branding) via the mozconfig;
                        this patch covers the few hardcoded chrome strings. Preference-level
                        brand values (update channel, theme) live in the 0002 pref block.
Files changed:          browser/base/content/aboutDialog.xhtml
Security impact:        None. Cosmetic strings only.
Performance impact:     None.
Upstream compatibility: aboutDialog.xhtml structure is stable; context verified against the
                        release branch (line ~42-45). Rebase risk LOW.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/aboutDialog.xhtml b/browser/base/content/aboutDialog.xhtml
--- a/browser/base/content/aboutDialog.xhtml
+++ b/browser/base/content/aboutDialog.xhtml
@@ -42,3 +42,7 @@
       <vbox id="leftBox" flex="1"/>
       <vbox id="rightBox">
+        <!-- STGR: always attribute the upstream base. -->
+        <description id="stgrUpstreamAttribution"
+                     class="stgr-attribution"
+                     value="Based on Mozilla Firefox"/>
         <label id="release" hidden="true">
